## **Toast** 

→ [NUXT UI 3.3](https://ui.nuxt.com/components/toast#usage)

### The Toast component provides non-intrusive, transient notifications to inform users about system events, errors, or user actions (e.g. success messages, warnings, or alerts). It should be simple to trigger, customizable, and stackable.

[https://www.figma.com/design/92moLelAY8lh8mI0rhCGzy/laioutr-UI?node-id=1-40](https://www.figma.com/design/92moLelAY8lh8mI0rhCGzy/laioutr-UI?node-id=1-40) 

| **Variants**: neutral success warning error **Properties**: orientation: vertical / horizontal boolean:  show icon show buttons has subline  | ![](blob:https://media.staging.atl-paas.net/?type=file&localId=null&id=f898a4b9-5357-43e4-97df-5ad4da2e4909&&collection=&height=900&occurrenceKey=null&width=583&__contextId=null&__displayType=null&__external=false&__fileMimeType=null&__fileName=null&__fileSize=null&__mediaTraceId=null&url=null)  |
| --- | --- |
| **Trigger by API or component usage** **Auto-dismissable** after a configurable duration **Manual dismiss (close button)** **Stackable** — supports multiple toasts shown simultaneously **Positioning** — top-right by default; configurable (e.g., bottom-left) **Transition animations** – slide in matching the direction of positioning on the screen (e.g., position is bottom right → slide in from right; position is bottom center-> slide in from bottom to top and so on) **Queue limit** — **optional** max number of concurrent toasts **Pause on hover** **Progress bar** to indicate time remaining **Icons per variant** (e.g., checkmark for success) **Rich content support** — allow for HTML or component slots **Accessibility (a11y)** — proper ARIA roles, keyboard navigation support Toasts should **not block user interaction** **On mobile:** adapt position and spacing for small screens only top or bottom positioning Animations should feel quick but smooth (e.g., 200–300ms) |  |
